## Objective
Implement and evaluate the section 3.2 coupled gradient estimator in a CPU numerical study of the synthetic IV model. The estimator itself, its iteration, and conclusions are intentionally not supplied. Treat the equations below as the fixed method specification; implement them independently.

## Fixed object and method
For `Z in R^(n x q)`, `X in R^(n x p)`, and `Y in R^n`, define the least-squares first-stage coefficient `Theta_hat = argmin_T ||Z T - X||_F^2` and 2SLS reference `beta_2SLS = argmin_b ||Z Theta_hat b - Y||_2^2` (no intercept). Initialize `beta^(0)=0` and `Theta^(0)=0`. At iteration `t`, using the same pre-update state `(beta^(t), Theta^(t))`, compute

`beta^(t+1) = beta^(t) - alpha (Theta^(t))^T Z^T (Z Theta^(t) beta^(t) - Y)`

`Theta^(t+1) = Theta^(t) - eta Z^T (Z Theta^(t) - X)`.

